enfs-dkms (0.1.3-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Actually-installable .deb (verified by `apt install` on a fresh
    24.04 VM, then `dkms status` showing `installed` and
    `modprobe enfs` succeeding).
  * 0.1.1 and 0.1.2 had a packaging bug: dh_dkms wasn't called with
    `-V`, so the #MODULE_VERSION# placeholder was shipped literally
    in /usr/src/enfs-#MODULE_VERSION#/dkms.conf and the post-install
    `dkms add` failed. Fixed in #4 by overriding dh_dkms.
  * Use this release; do not use 0.1.1 or 0.1.2.

 -- Darren <darren@example.invalid>  Sat, 02 May 2026 11:00:00 +0200

enfs-dkms (0.1.2-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Fix DKMS install: dh_dkms needs the full dkms.conf with
    #MODULE_VERSION# placeholder, not a 4-line stub. Without this fix
    `apt install enfs-dkms_0.1.1-1_amd64.deb` succeeded but the
    post-install `dkms add` failed with "directory
    /var/lib/dkms/enfs/#MODULE_VERSION#/source does not appear to
    have module source located within it". 0.1.2 is the first .deb
    that actually installs cleanly.
  * Builds and loads end-to-end on:
      - Ubuntu 26.04 LTS         (kernel 7.0)        [GA]
      - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS HWE     (kernel 6.14)
      - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS GA      (kernel 6.8)

 -- Darren <darren@example.invalid>  Sat, 02 May 2026 10:41:38 +0200

enfs-dkms (0.1.1-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * First usable release. Builds and loads end-to-end on:
      - Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (kernel 7.0)
      - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS HWE (kernel 6.14)
      - Ubuntu 24.04 LTS GA (kernel 6.8)
  * 4-path multipath mount verified on 7.0 (25/25/25/25 load split
    across four NFS backends) and on 6.8 + 6.14 (xprt switch shows
    N active transports, pm_ping monitors all paths).
  * GitHub Actions CI: build matrix across all three targets plus
    a lintian-clean .deb build, gated by branch protection on main.
  * Tagged v* releases auto-publish the .deb via the release
    workflow.

 -- Darren <darren@example.invalid>  Sat, 02 May 2026 10:26:11 +0200

enfs-dkms (0.1.0-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Initial scaffold.
    - Vendor OpenEuler OLK-6.6 enfs sources under vendor/openeuler/.
    - DKMS skeleton (dkms.conf.in, three BUILT_MODULE_* slots).
    - Out-of-tree Kbuild stub.
    - Compat header at compat/enfs_compat.h.
    - Sync / port / deploy / dkms-install scripts.
    - Architecture, porting and DKMS docs.
    - Not yet buildable - see docs/PORTING-NOTES.md.

